{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the fountains of the deep were stopped up.</b> Rashi explains: some of them remained for the world's needs, such as the hot springs of Tiberias. And if you ask: according to the one who says the Flood did not fall upon the land of Israel, from where did the hot springs of Tiberias come there, seeing that they are in the land of Israel? One may answer: there are fountains of the deep throughout the entire world, and it is written 'all the fountains of the deep were broken open' — this implies even in the land of Israel, and from there the hot springs of Tiberias remained." "<b>And the fountains were stopped up, etc.</b> This verse is not in its proper place; rather, after 'And the Flood was forty, etc.' it should have written 'and the fountains were stopped up,' and after it 'and the waters receded, etc.' Rather, Scripture wished to arrange and combine all the matters that caused the diminishing of the waters."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:24.966052332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}